# milestone 28 / story 00 — the SEA build recipe's local output (esbuild bundle,
# sidecar assets, sea-config.json, blob, and the built binary). A generated
# artifact, never committed; Story 01's CI matrix produces the signed release
# artifacts separately.
dist-sea/

# story 125 — the staged site `scripts/site/build-site.mjs` assembles for the Pages
# workflow: the committed docs/ shell plus the pages it projects from their committed
# sources (the loop graph document, the planning PRDs). Rebuilt on every deploy, never
# committed — a committed copy of the graph page is the drift the site exists to remove. The
# `.dist-site-*` sibling is the builder's atomic-swap staging; a hard kill mid-swap strands one.
dist-site/
.dist-site-*/

# Runtime: live agent-terminal session registry (operational, not committed)
.aof/terminal-sessions.json

# NOTE: the mesh record stream (.aof/mesh/) is ignored in .aof/.gitignore, alongside
# the other .aof/ runtime/derived state — not here.

# milestone 36 / story 00 — the Rust Cargo build output for the Mesh Desktop App
# (app/desktop/). Cargo.lock IS committed (an application workspace, not a published
# library) — only the compiled target/ artifact directory is generated/ignored.
app/desktop/target/

# milestone 36 / stories 01-02 — the Tauri shell (crates/app/) is EXCLUDED from the
# app/desktop/ Cargo workspace (its own independent build), so it gets its own
# target/ output dir; and crates/app/gen/ is Tauri's own build-script-generated
# schema/capability output (regenerated every build, never hand-edited).
app/desktop/crates/app/target/
app/desktop/crates/app/gen/

MicrosoftEdgeWebview2Setup.exe 

# aof mesh runtime: per-run git worktrees the worker daemon checks out to execute
# assigned items — a full embedded checkout of this repo, never a record to commit.
# (m43's bundle .gitignore stopped blanket-ignoring .aof/mesh/ because on a real node
# the mesh dir IS the tracked bus; the worktrees under it are still runtime state.)
.aof/mesh/worktrees/
# milestone 50 / story 03 — the SESSION lane's own worktree root, a deliberate SIBLING of
# the assignment lane's above (TECH_DEBT item 47): the assignment startup-reclaim scan
# enumerates `worktrees/` and trusts every directory name it finds there as an
# assignmentId, so a launched operator shell's tree must never materialize inside it.
.aof/mesh/session-worktrees/
# story 65 / task 02 — the LOCAL DISPATCH lane's own worktree root, the third sibling
# (never a child of either of the two above, for the same TECH_DEBT 47 reason). One tree
# per concurrently-dispatched story, so two independent story builds can never share a
# working tree — measured necessity, not hardening: in vista-app-web 352 two stories the
# architect had partitioned as independent both edited one file, ×9 and ×8.
.aof/mesh/dispatch-worktrees/

# The private downstream project names this repo must not disclose. The LIST is the sensitive
# part, so it never lands in a commit; .githooks/pre-commit and acd-no-internal-project-names
# both SKIP without it (guard-if-present).
.aof/private-terms.json

# story 83 / F-83-F — `aof work observe --write` derives a per-item snapshot from Claude Code
# session transcripts into `<item>/observability/`. The report's own header calls it "a diagnostic,
# not a work record — safe to delete or .gitignore", and no snapshot has ever been committed. The
# finding it closes was a hygiene one discharged by MOVING files into a folder named `_to_delete`,
# which reads as progress to a human and as nothing at all to git: the mechanism is the rule, not
# the intention.
wiki/work/**/observability/
